{
  "id": "ep185",
  "duration": 52.716,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.848,
      "text": "Exposing your body to space will never make you explode.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Nicole Stott participates in the STS-128 mission's first spacewalk.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nicole_Stott_participates_in_the_STS-128_mission%27s_first_spacewalk.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 2.067,
          "end": 3.833,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.848,
      "end": 9.918,
      "text": "Sci-fi films depict violent ruptures, but human skin easily prevents you from bursting.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.833,
          "end": 9.933,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.918,
      "end": 16.188,
      "text": "Instant freezing is impossible too, since a vacuum only sheds heat slowly through radiation.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.933,
          "end": 16.2,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 16.188,
      "end": 22.313,
      "text": "Instead, ebullism forms gas bubbles in your tissues, swelling you up to twice your size.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Art Institute of Chicago (CC0)",
        "title": "The Fall of the Giants",
        "credit": "Salvator Rosa\nItalian, 1615-1673",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/16"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 16.2,
          "end": 22.3,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 22.313,
      "end": 27.833,
      "text": "Worse, your lungs reverse function, actively stripping oxygen right out of your blood.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "XBio illustration \u2013 Gas Exchange.png",
        "credit": "explorebiology",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Gas_Exchange.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 22.3,
          "end": 27.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 27.833,
      "end": 35.328,
      "text": "In the mid-1960s, NASA technician Jim LeBlanc accidentally depressurized inside a vacuum chamber.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Space Environment Simulation Chamber, NASA, Houston (Harris County, Texas).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA photographer",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Space_Environment_Simulation_Chamber,_NASA,_Houston_(Harris_County,_Texas).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 27.833,
          "end": 35.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 35.328,
      "end": 41.328,
      "text": "Conscious for about fifteen seconds, his last memory was saliva bubbling on his tongue.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Art Institute of Chicago (CC0)",
        "title": "Face",
        "credit": "Artist unknown (Teotihuacan)\nTeotihuacan, Vallery of Mexico, Mexico",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/212967"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 35.333,
          "end": 38.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 38.867,
          "end": 41.333,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 41.328,
      "end": 47.248,
      "text": "Crews repressurized the room within thirty seconds, leaving him without any permanent damage.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NPP Runs the Gauntlet of Environmental Testing (GSFC 20171208 Archive e001819).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Goddard Space Flight Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NPP_Runs_the_Gauntlet_of_Environmental_Testing_(GSFC_20171208_Archive_e001819).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 41.333,
          "end": 43.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 43.4,
          "end": 47.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 47.248,
      "end": 52.366,
      "text": "You have roughly ninety seconds before hypoxia kills you, not a cinematic blast.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Nicole Stott participates in the STS-128 mission's first spacewalk.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nicole_Stott_participates_in_the_STS-128_mission%27s_first_spacewalk.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 47.233,
          "end": 52.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
